#
# LEGEND: This DTR defines a canonical hexagonal-architecture application
# following LLMDD conventions.
#
# Layer structure (domain → application → infrastructure → control):
#   DOMAIN.models          — domain models (entities, value objects)
#   APPLICATION.ports      — port interfaces (driven/driving)
#   APPLICATION.services   — business logic services
#   APPLICATION.use_cases  — use case orchestrators
#   INFRASTRUCTURE.<feature> — adapters grouped by feature
#   CONTROL.cli              — CLI parsing
#   CONTROL.dependency_injection — DI container wiring
#   CONTROL.entry_point      — application entry point
#
# Naming conventions:
#   - No Impl, Port, Service suffixes on classes/modules
#   - Folder structure tells the role (port vs service vs adapter)

ARCH=HEX,DI,DIP,NO_CROSS_LAYER,PORT_FLOW_OUT_IN,DOTENV_WALKUP,CODER_FEEDBACK,SEVERITY,ITR_LIFECYCLE,HARD_FAIL
